# =============================================================================
# Nothing in this list is ever committed.
#
# Two rules behind it:
#
# 1. Runtime state never goes in git. Worlds, player data, plugin jars, generated
#    configs and logs are produced on a player's machine, and a world is tens of
#    gigabytes of somebody else's work.
# 2. Credentials never go in git. Not encrypted, not "just this once". A secret
#    that reaches a remote can be assumed leaked, and rewriting history does not
#    un-clone a repository.
#
# Each rule below is tested by agent/tests/test_gitignore.py, so a pattern that
# stops working is a failing test rather than a leak.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Runtime state ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# The server directory for a checkout at the repository root.
/server/

# A server started by the agent, wherever the operator put it. The agent's own
# data directory holds worlds, player data, plugin jars, generated configs, the
# per-server RCON password and the agent's logs.
/agent/data/
/agent/logs/

# Backups produced by `mc backup`.
/backups/

# Per-machine heap overrides. Written by the agent from the dashboard's memory
# settings, or edited by hand.
/server.env

# Console FIFO and pid file. Both live inside /server but are called out so an
# accidental `git add -f` is obvious.
*.pid
*.fifo

# ---- Credentials ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# /agent/agent.json holds the one-time agent token. It is a credential that
# grants control of the machine the agent runs on.
/agent/agent.json

# Environment files. `.env.example` is deliberately re-included below, because a
# committed example is documentation, not a secret.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.*.example

# Keys and certificates. Private key formats only -- a `.crt` is often committed
# on purpose as part of a public certificate chain.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.truststore
*.asc
*.gpg
*.kdbx
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ecdsa
id_ecdsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
id_dsa
id_dsa.*

# A tunnel provider's claim token, if an operator keeps one here rather than in
# agent.json. Belt and braces: agent.json is ignored, but so is a stray copy.
*.claim-token

# ---- Build artefacts --------------------------------------------------------
#
# Minecraft itself, Paper, Geyser and Floodgate are not redistributed here;
# `mc install` fetches them at pinned, checksum-verified versions. The same goes
# for plugin jars an operator drops in. A jar in this repository is always
# either a mistake or something that should have been fetched, never source.
*.jar
*.war
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# ---- Noise ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Python bytecode from running the bridge, the agent and their tests.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]